{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-syntomic}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1a311bbc38d2ac77783bc2a3e922a9cf45fd93c6bbcc4fb173ba25bc7c898945", "source_text": "Syntomic topology", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9f88f4a68f4ee1d009cbeba8193006c64e5fa46a97e6cdcd38ddba6f1f367425", "unit_id": "tag:03YA:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-section-syntomic}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:a2ca825660cbae38997e7e969f00199e361a5cc0c9c747c267879260e8258ffa", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we discuss the notion of a syntomic covering of\nalgebraic spaces, and we define the big syntomic site of an\nalgebraic space. Please compare with\nTopologies, Section <REF_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c859e2f38b24243cf2e7ce06e6e3ef804e01867d388d078caf48b773b548f097", "unit_id": "tag:03YA:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{f_i : X_i \\to X\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0006": "$S$", "MATH_0007": "$f_i$", "MATH_0008": "$$\n|X| = \\bigcup\\nolimits_{i \\in I} |f_i|(|X_i|),\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-syntomic-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e76fae56c3226e3151fabee0092a70b466b5acf08f6f31c1ff32db92d85286f7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:208e5e5fec903b6995006d17fce5cc981d6e48ffe65bf459efd1dc7abaa4144e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>syntomic covering of <MATH_0004><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family of morphisms\n<MATH_0005> of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0006>\nsuch that each <MATH_0007> is syntomic\nand such that\n<MATH_0008>\ni.e., the morphisms are jointly surjective.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7acb6553872c5895029cc19f14f41d4510e2a992b5b1df85ddacde2dd632474f", "unit_id": "tag:041A:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X_i$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-syntomic-covering}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:471134057d0984d44af5a155ac2d0e8da290e691491a26f5be3167e4b5c64d48", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c84e05e96c1eda67f90e73cb2d727ae434ffe70e2511856709141cebc8f4a5e5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis is exactly the same as\nTopologies, Definition <REF_0001>.\nIn particular, if <MATH_0001> and all the <MATH_0002> are schemes, then we recover the\nusual notion of a syntomic covering of schemes.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e4ff9e444dbcb34621071e44dfea349f181b23b06c65f7d882ebef0b3220f512", "unit_id": "tag:03YA:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:18d9c47d4862d33cf3e32e9e58cc9c68c1600e6612ee824428f510847301a3ce", "source_text": "Any smooth covering is a syntomic covering, and a fortiori,\nany <ACCENT_0001>tale or Zariski covering is a syntomic covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5e992b61018e19a519ab5721940331afe1c17648721d9172c38a9b17b795b167", "unit_id": "tag:0DFB:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{spaces-morphisms-lemma-smooth-syntomic}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-zariski-etale-smooth}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b5a9801c3f1a53ea753cc888586cfba03a19e1224abbeed135ff177bd4313ff", "source_text": "This is clear from the definitions and the fact that a smooth\nmorphism is syntomic\n(Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <REF_0001>),\nand Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7a92ba029160f0f59572dd35b38750b6e993b9c3676ffd140a05542118e91833", "unit_id": "tag:0DFB:proof"}
{"chapter": "spaces-topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03YA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{X' \\to X\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$i$", "MATH_0009": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X_i\\}_{j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\{X_{ij} \\to X\\}_{i \\in I, j\\in J_i}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\{X_i \\to X\\}_{i\\in I}$", "MATH_0012": "$X' \\to X$", "MATH_0013": "$\\{X' \\times_X X_i \\to X'\\}_{i\\in I}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-syntomic}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9e3d9a30bc295880eafea81ddede5c59549b2394c91422582e284bba1fee4680", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9dd91559be7d3ba7d73c5764ad39e90b82d1216c4e3131726d45b397026e18d5", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> If <MATH_0004> is an isomorphism then <MATH_0005>\nis a syntomic covering of <MATH_0006>.\n<STRUCT_0003> If <MATH_0007> is a syntomic covering and for each\n<MATH_0008> we have a syntomic covering <MATH_0009>, then\n<MATH_0010> is a syntomic covering.\n<STRUCT_0004> If <MATH_0011> is a syntomic covering\nand <MATH_0012> is a morphism of algebraic spaces then\n<MATH_0013> is a syntomic covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6556dbd90df1bee526cd0e89a66e138587c0d7d17a6a362f1171db5c25b2f1f6", "unit_id": "tag:041B:statement"}
